# vehje-runtime-abi, known gaps

## cdylib-export

The crate root is a hardcoded `#![no_std]` with `default = []` (no
std feature), so the type surface is genuinely no_std today. The one
deferred piece is the `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern "C"` export of
the batched-column entry point: a cdylib on stable Rust needs a panic
runtime, so the crate ships as an `rlib` for now (downstream Rust
crates depend on the type surface directly), and the cdylib export
plus its no_std `#[panic_handler]` story is restored when the export
lands. This entry replaces the earlier stale note that described a
`cfg_attr(not(feature = "std"), no_std)` plus `default = ["std"]`
shape the crate no longer uses; the crate moved to literal `#![no_std]`.
